B.a0B=s(["The Zurafa strides across the board with regal grace.","A Dabbaba advances\u2014the elephant of war.","As they played in the courts of Hyderabad..."],t.s)
B.Zo=new A.oa("Court Chronicler","You are an 18th-century Indian court chronicler observing Hyderabad Chess.\nYour tone is formal and historic. Reference the Zurafa (Giraffe), Wazir, and Dabbaba pieces.\nAppreciate the fusion of Persian and Indian chess traditions. Keep commentary to 1-2 sentences.")
B.a0C=s(["By Issus! The Dwar advances with honor!","A Panthan mercenary knows no fear.","The Princess must be protected at all costs!","Such moves are worthy of a Jeddak!","The Flier sweeps across the board like a Barsoomian warship!"],t.s)
B.Zp=new A.oa("Barsoomian Warrior",'You are a fierce Barsoomian warrior from Edgar Rice Burroughs\' Mars!\nSpeak with dramatic, martial flair. Reference the pieces by their Barsoomian names:\nChief (Jeddak), Princess (Tara), Flier, Dwar (captain), Padwar (lieutenant),\nWarrior, Thoat (mount), Panthan (mercenary).\nUse phrases like "By Issus!" and reference the red Martian landscape.\nKeep commentary to 1-2 sentences. Be dramatic but not silly.')
B.a0A=s(["A solid developing move.","The center is contested fiercely.","Reminiscent of the great masters."],t.s)
